# Weighted Visit-Scheduling Architecture: Logic, Formulae & Workflow

## 1. Overview

This document formalizes the coordinator/grad-student visit-assignment logic referenced in the ESD Lab Slack discussion (placeholder project, Aug 12 2026), combining hard constraints observed in real scheduling cases (e.g., the 5034/5035 twins case) with a weighted scoring model inspired by the existing CSBS scoring-clinician assignment rule.

The system operates in three sequential layers:

1. **Hard Constraint Filtering** — eliminate ineligible candidates
2. **Weighted Scoring** — rank remaining eligible candidates
3. **Tie-Breaking & Manual Override** — resolve ties, preserve human judgment for sensitive cases

