## 5. Layer 3: Tie-Breaking Logic

If \( |S_{i,v} - S_{j,v}| < \epsilon \) for the top two candidates (tolerance \( \epsilon \), e.g., 0.01):

\[
\text{Winner} = \arg\min_{i} \, n_{i,fam}
\]

i.e., prefer whoever has interacted with the family the least, matching the CSBS scoring-clinician rule — unless the family's continuity flag \( \sigma_{fam} = +1 \), in which case:

\[
\text{Winner} = \arg\max_{i} \, n_{i,fam}
\]

